      "worked_solution": "The point $A$ on the graph has coordinates $(0,1).$ Therefore:\n\n$$\nf(0)=1\n$$\n\nApplying ${f}^{-1}$ to both sides of the above equation, and using the fact that ${f}^{-1}(f(x))=x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{-1}(f(0)) & ={f}^{-1}(1) \\\\ 0 & ={f}^{-1}(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that ${f}^{-1}(1)=0.$",
